==Overview==
<tabber>
Pros=
{{Overview|Pros
|'''General'''
* Much greater [[Flash Step]] range and cooldown reduction.
* Great pick for glass cannon or highly aggressive builds.

|'''[[Last Resort]] (V3)'''
* Could be an alternative to [[Cyborg]]'s Energy Core for one-shot combos.
* Great damage (from 50% HP or lower).

|'''Psycho (V4)'''
* Insane mobility, useful for chasing enemies or evading.
* Allows you to play hyper-aggressive by dashing around your opponent to intimidate and damage
* Tier 2 comes with uncancellable attacks, making it extremely useful against anything with tick damage (e.g: T-Rex's Prey Mark, Infernal Pincer's burn damage and [[Cyborg]] as a whole).

|'''Limit Break (V4)'''
* Insane damage potential, when at high percentages, it is possible to do upwards of 7k damage (in a single hit) using the right move.
* Makes dealing with teamers much easier because of the high damage output requiring less moves to be landed in order to get a kill.
}}


|-|Cons=
{{Overview|Cons
|'''General'''
* More focused towards damage and flash step, mostly accompanying one playstyle that may not be for everyone.

|'''[[Last Resort]] (V3)'''
* Can be risky in PvP, making the player vulnerable while they are at low HP for extra damage.
* Requires the user to already be losing the fight to use to its full extent.

|'''Psycho (V4)'''
* Still can be seen by [[Instinct]].

|'''Limit Break (V4)'''
* Takes a while to deal a large amount of damage.
}}
</tabber>

==Notes==
* Combining Human with the [[Kitsune Ribbon]] lowers the player's [[Flash Step]] cooldown to 7.5 seconds.
** However, Psycho (both Tier 1 and 2) while in V4 isn't affected by the buffs granted by the accessory.
* Human grants the user a permanent extra dodge for [[Instinct]].
* Human can deal insane damage when used with high combo potential fruits like [[Dough]] or [[Magnet|Magnet.]]
* The Human race, along with the [[Cyborg]] race, are the only races that do not provide buffs to the user on V1.

